--!strict
-- The sixteen personalities a villager can have. Traits run 0..1 and steer which random events a
-- villager starts and how they react to them.
--   social    how often they seek others out
--   temper    how easily they fall out with someone
--   kind      how often they help, share and make up
--   mischief  pranks, teasing, wandering off
--   lazy      naps, skipped chores, skipped turns
--   brave     charges in, protects friends
--   focus     sticks to the plan (high) or does something random (low)
-- `lines` is their own voice, by kind: hello, happy, sad, angry, thanks (the speech bubbles and
-- Sim/Talk), and the reactions the events reach for (Data/Events/Kit's s:voice): wow, scared,
-- sorry, yes, no, bye, tease, brag, worry, hmm, excited, tired, laugh. So the same event sounds
-- different with a shy villager in it than with a loud one.
-- They talk the way a friend texts you (the user gave us a messaging app's chats to learn from:
-- their feel only, never a line of them). A line is a message or two of about six words, and each
-- personality is built from two or three strong habits and little else: the sunny ones shout half
-- the time and the cool ones never, the shy and gloomy ones trail off in "...", the cheeky ones
-- laugh in lower case, the dramatic ones put one word in capitals.
-- `{player}` is the player's name (the user: "the player is to be referred to as their player
-- name"), filled in where the line is said: about one line in seven, mostly first. It goes in the
-- kinds a villager says to the player or in front of them (happy, sad, wow, scared, worry, brag,
-- excited, tired), never in the ones said to another villager in an event (hello, thanks, sorry,
-- tease, yes, no and the rest).

export type Personality = {
	id: string,
	name: string,
	blurb: string,
	traits: { [string]: number },
	color: string,
	lines: { [string]: { string } },
}

